{"x":5,"y":"8","captures":[[{"rule":0,"flash":[],"flips":[]},{"rule":3,"flash":[],"flips":[]}]],"p1s":5,"p2s":5,"eb":0,"z":"Ymx1ZQ==/715620474636505724222b404b6e294b3b675051672c362e5176412d64","u":2,"c":"14","dialog":[[{"buttons":[{"name":"Skip Tutorial","link":"0"},{"name":"Start Tutorial","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Welcome to the Plus Tutorial.</p><p>Would you like to see a quick demonstration about how the rule works?</p>"},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Okay","direction":1}],"content":"<p>The Plus rule works a lot like the Same rule but instead of comparing equal ranks, it compares the sum of ranks.</p><p>Add together the rank of your played card with the adjacent rank. If its sum is equal to the sum on one of the other sides, then all cards involved are captured.</p><p>Let's have look!</p>"}],[]],"gameover":[]}
